 DemoAutoConf connected;mkbox;COORD;LF
⍝ Demonstrates the Attach and AutoConf properties. The CENTER test pane
⍝ (F1.RIGHT.BOT) is bordered by a splitter on two orthogonal sides — a VERTICAL
⍝ splitter on its left (drag = width) and a HORIZONTAL splitter on its top
⍝ (drag = height) — so it can be resized in both axes and every labelled box
⍝ inside reconfigures per its Attach edges (gated by its AutoConf). Resizing
⍝ width exercises the Left/Right edges; resizing height exercises Top/Bottom.
⍝ The left strip contrasts pinned / proportional / AutoConf 3-vs-0.
⍝ NB: EWC splitters are form-relative, so they nest at most one level cleanly;
⍝ this two-splitter layout is the robust way to resize a pane in both axes.
 EWC.CONNECTED←connected
 ⎕PW←1000
 COORD←'Pixel'
 LF←⎕UCS 10   ⍝ a newline in a Label caption makes it wrap (else it clips)

⍝ mkbox ⍵ = (name caption Posn Size BCol Attach AutoConf) -> a coloured,
⍝ bordered SubForm "box" with a wrapping caption Label filling it.
⍝ NB: each eWC is assigned (_←) so the dfn does not return early on the first
⍝ bare expression.
 mkbox←{
     (nm cap P S C A ac)←⍵
     _←nm eWC'SubForm'('Posn' P)('Size' S)('BCol' C)('EdgeStyle' 'Border')('Attach' A)('AutoConf' ac)
     _←(nm,'.CAP')eWC'Label' cap(3 4)((¯6+1⊃S),(¯8+2⊃S))
     0
 }

⍝ Form is 800x800 to match the Splitter's pane sizing.
 'F1'eWC'Form' 'AutoConf and Attach'(0 0)(800 800)('Coord' COORD)

⍝ === Panes: LEFT strip | RIGHT, and RIGHT split into a top hint strip + the
⍝ CENTER test pane. Two splitters => the test pane resizes in both axes. =======
 'F1.LEFT'eWC'SubForm'('Posn'(0 0))('Size'(800 240))('BCol'(245 245 245))
 'F1.RIGHT'eWC'SubForm'('Posn'(0 243))('Size'(800 557))('BCol'(250 250 250))
 'F1.SPLIT'eWC'Splitter' 'F1.LEFT' 'F1.RIGHT'('Posn'(0 240))

 'F1.RIGHT.TOP'eWC'SubForm'('Posn'(0 0))('Size'(100 557))('BCol'(235 240 245))
 'F1.RIGHT.BOT'eWC'SubForm'('Posn'(103 0))('Size'(697 557))('BCol'(255 255 255))
 'F1.RIGHT.SPLIT'eWC'Splitter'('SplitObj1' 'F1.RIGHT.TOP')('SplitObj2' 'F1.RIGHT.BOT')('Style' 'Horz')('Posn'(100 0))

⍝ Hints in the top strip so it's clear which splitter does what.
 'F1.RIGHT.TOP.H1'eWC'Label' ('↔  Vertical splitter (left) — drag to resize the test pane WIDTH')(14 12)(18 530)
 'F1.RIGHT.TOP.H2'eWC'Label' ('↕  Horizontal splitter (above) — drag to resize the test pane HEIGHT')(40 12)(18 530)

⍝ === CENTER test pane: window-frame edge anchoring =============================
⍝ All default AutoConf 3, so only Attach differs. Resize the pane in either axis.
 mkbox 'F1.RIGHT.BOT.TB'('Toolbar',LF,'Top Left Top Right')(6 6)(34 545)(200 220 255)('Top' 'Left' 'Top' 'Right')3
 mkbox 'F1.RIGHT.BOT.LB'('Left side',LF,'Top Left Bottom Left')(46 6)(605 110)(255 245 200)('Top' 'Left' 'Bottom' 'Left')3
 mkbox 'F1.RIGHT.BOT.CF'('Center fill',LF,'Top Left Bottom Right')(46 122)(605 313)(225 210 255)('Top' 'Left' 'Bottom' 'Right')3
 mkbox 'F1.RIGHT.BOT.RB'('Right side',LF,'Top Right Bottom Right')(46 441)(605 110)(255 220 190)('Top' 'Right' 'Bottom' 'Right')3
 mkbox 'F1.RIGHT.BOT.SB'('Status bar',LF,'Bottom Left Bottom Right')(657 6)(34 545)(200 255 200)('Bottom' 'Left' 'Bottom' 'Right')3

⍝ === LEFT strip: AutoConf contrast + pinned + proportional ====================
⍝ This strip resizes horizontally (via the vertical splitter F1.SPLIT).
 'F1.LEFT.TITLE'eWC'Label' 'AutoConf + Attach'(8 10)(20 220)
 'F1.LEFT.I1'eWC'Label' ('Drag either splitter to',LF,'resize the test pane →')(30 10)(32 225)

 mkbox 'F1.LEFT.PIN'('Pinned',LF,'Top Left Top Left')(70 10)(52 200)(255 210 225)('Top' 'Left' 'Top' 'Left')3
 mkbox 'F1.LEFT.PROP'('Proportional',LF,'None x4 (scales)')(130 10)(60 220)(200 245 245)('None' 'None' 'None' 'None')3

 'F1.LEFT.ACLBL'eWC'Label' 'Same Attach, different AutoConf:'(200 10)(30 225)
 mkbox 'F1.LEFT.AC3'('AutoConf 3',LF,'accepts → stretches')(235 10)(50 220)(200 245 200)('Top' 'Left' 'Top' 'Right')3
 mkbox 'F1.LEFT.AC0'('AutoConf 0',LF,'ignores → frozen')(295 10)(50 220)(255 205 205)('Top' 'Left' 'Top' 'Right')0

 :If ~connected
     ⎕EX 'F1.HR'
 :EndIf
